<title>UK: Mexico 500 bln lire bond due this week - dealers.</title>
<headline>Mexico 500 bln lire bond due this week - dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's expected 500 billion lire 10-year Eurobond was due to be launched this week, dealers said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;The focus this week will be on the Mexico deal, which is already oversubscribed, and is likely to be blow-out,&quot; said a syndicate manager at a European bank.</p>
<p>Spread talk was just above 200 basis points over BTPs, dealers said. Chase was tipped as lead manager.</p>
<p>Mexico launched a $1.0 billion 10-year global bond at the start of January. Issued to yield 335 b.p. over U.S. Treasuries, the bond was trading at just under 300 b.p. over.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
